<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Fitzgerald returns one week after her first visit and is seen by Dr. Langford of the coordinated specialty care team on the same day. She takes risperidone 2 mg every night. She sleeps nine or ten hours and feels heavy and slow in the mornings. She has had no voices, no sense of being watched, and no racing thoughts. Her mood is still low but less tearful, and she has begun writing again for an hour a day. Her periods have still not returned; she has had no breast discharge. She is eating three small meals and has not danced. She is worried that medicines will make her gain weight and end her dancing. She has had no thoughts of suicide or self-harm. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Risperidone</td><td>2 mg at bedtime, every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Psychotic and manic symptoms</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Low but improving; PHQ-9 9; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Nine or ten hours; slow in the mornings</td></tr><tr><td>Periods</td><td>Still absent; no breast discharge</td></tr><tr><td>Concern</td><td>Weight gain and her dancing</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

